# Dev Notes 42 — Capability Bus Execute Action Contract v1

**Date:** 2026-06-16  
**Branch:** `capability-bus-execute-action-contract-v1`  
**Status:** Final candidate package validated for `capability-bus-execute-action-contract-v1`: assistant sandbox checks, contract-smoke checks, helper checks, artifact guard, package extraction/recheck, and Michael-run local checks passed. This candidate document intentionally does not assert branch-upload, repo-verification, merge, or main-verification status; record those separately after direct GitHub verification. No real-runtime test required while the diff remains contract-only and avoids runtime/worker/lifecycle/native execution surfaces.

---

## 1. Purpose

This branch adds the first contract-only Capability Bus execute-action seam under:

```text
runtime/bus/executeAction/
```

The branch defines how a validated action envelope flows through the existing contract chain and becomes an accepted metadata-only execute-action descriptor:

```text
action envelope
  -> Capability Bus intake
  -> Capability Router route plan
  -> Capability Service plan
  -> Backend Adapter plan
  -> Capability Execution descriptor
  -> Capability Bus execute-action accepted descriptor/result/event metadata
```

This is not real execution. It does not invoke services, call backend adapters, enqueue runtime requests, stream tokens, route `prompt()` through the bus, or expose `executeAction()` through `runtime.mjs`.

