## 7. Contract-only guardrails

The branch preserves these boundaries:

```text
runtime.mjs public export set unchanged
prompt() behavior unchanged
workerBridge unchanged
llama_worker unchanged
scheduler unchanged
request lifecycle unchanged
stream shaping unchanged
config/configOverride unchanged
model identity/path guardrails unchanged
runtime/execution/ remains descriptor-only
```

The new execute-action modules avoid imports of:

```text
runtime.mjs
workerBridge
llama_worker
node-llama-cpp
worker_threads
child_process
scheduler/request internals
ReadableStream
```

Validation failures are propagated through the existing contract validators with execute-action-specific prefixes.

Forbidden executable/backend-private payloads continue to be rejected through upstream contract validators, including payloads such as:

```text
modelPath/baseModel/mmprojPath/projectorPath
backendOptions/adapterArgs/rawBackendPayload
toolProcess/command/shell/exec/spawn/cwd/env/stdio
function/handler/execute/executeAction/invoke
workerBridge/llama_worker/nodeLlamaCpp
```

